<title>AUSTRALIA: Reserve Bank of Australia commodity index falls.</title>
<headline>Reserve Bank of Australia commodity index falls.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank of Australia said its index  of commodity prices fell by 1.3 percent in Special Drawing Rights  (SDR) terms in July after falling 3.1 percent in June.</p>
<p>Falls in the prices of wool, wheat and gold were partly offset by  higher prices for beef and aluminium.</p>
<p>In Australian dollar terms, the index fell by 0.6 percent after a  rise of 0.2 percent in June.</p>
<p>The Reserve Bank indices were as follows (base 1989/90):</p>
<p>		     All Items		   Non-Rural Component</p>
<p>		A$	SDR	US$	   A$	SDR	US$</p>
<p>July 97 p  94.6     85.5     91.2	 99.4     89.9     95.9</p>
<p>June 97 r  95.2     86.6     93.2	 98.9     90.0     96.9</p>
<p>July 96 r  93.1     85.1     95.5	 96.8     88.6     99.3</p>
<p>		 Rural Component		     Base Metals</p>
<p>		A$	SDR	US$	  A$	 SDR	US$</p>
<p>July 97 p  87.1     78.7     84.0	95.7	86.5     92.4</p>
<p>June 97 r  89.5     81.4     87.6	93.5	84.9     91.6</p>
<p>July 96 r  86.3     78.9     88.5	81.3	74.3     83.4</p>
<p>NOTE - r = revised, p = preliminary  </p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
